# netsurf: leaf elements in or out of a block-level flex box are placed alone too (patch 503)
# Generated 2026-11-28
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 502)
#
# Patch 502 places items in or out of a block-level flex box alone, but
# skipped the leaf (patch 407: between blocks) and late (patch 378:
# appended at the end) placements, so a new <img> or <iframe> still built
# the whole flex box again: stackoverflow inserts <iframe>s into its flex
# <body>, ~2,900 boxes each time. In a flex box the builder blockifies a
# replaced element -- its box lands straight under the flex box, as in a
# full build -- so both placements are allowed in 502's flex mode (the
# late one for iframes and images only), and the item is placed like any
# other. One that lands in a line instead is still a full reconvert at
# placement (502's guard, which now tests only where the box landed).
#
# Gate: JS-flex-leaf / CSS-flex-leaf-ref (an <img> and an <iframe> between
# items, each appended at the end, two <img>s side by side, an <input>
# appended -- the box built again whole -- and <img>s before and after
# whitespace), row for row against the same steps at parse time.
#
# Measured on stackoverflow: the iframe batches now get past placement and
# then meet a sibling-combinator rule over <body>'s children, which
# rebuilds the parent (446) -- still <body> whole -- so this alone does not
# change that page; see doc 10.
--- a/content/handlers/html/html.c
+++ b/content/handlers/html/html.c
@@ -10047,7 +10047,14 @@
